  "description": "WOQDUB crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: (C12 H35 Dy4 N3 O24 2+)n,2n(Cl1 O4 1-),10n(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2C (Dy) has 1 O neighbors; Dy3C (Dy) has 1 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 1 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 1 O neighbors; Dy4C (Dy) has 1 O neighbors; Dy1C (Dy) has 1 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 7 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.721-3.853 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.47-111.14°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula {[Dy4(μ3-OH)4(asp)3(H2O)8](ClO4)2·10H2O}n. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
